course: dictionary
lesson: 13324
title: A word that is not a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Gu» on its own is not an English word, so you will not find it in an English sentence by itself. When you meet a short piece like this, ask: is it a whole word, or a piece of a longer word? Look at the letters and words around it first.
explain: In Mandarin, a language spoken in China, «gu» is a syllable, which is a small unit of sound. Its meaning changes with its tone, the way your voice goes up, down or stays flat. «Gǔ» means old or ancient, as in «gǔdài», ancient times. «Gū» means aunt, your father's sister, as in «gūgu».
explain: The tone marks above the letters are the clue. The same sound with a different tone can mean something completely different, so read the marks carefully. In English texts, «gu» usually turns up as a piece cut from a longer word, such as gum or guide, or as part of a name like Gu.
fact: Gu is not a word in English on its own.
fact: In Mandarin, «gu» is a syllable, and its tone changes its meaning.
fact: «Gǔ» means old or ancient, or bone, or drum.
fact: «Gū» means aunt, your father's sister.
fact: «Gu» can be a surname, like the name Gu, and it sounds like «goo».
exercise: «Gǔdài» means ancient times, so gǔ in this word means what? | Sound like a goo | Aunt | Reason | *Old or ancient
exercise: Mei says, «Gū is my aunt on Dad's side.» What does gū mean? | Bone | Reason | A long way away | *Aunt, your father's sister
exercise: You see «gu» alone at the end of a line in an English book. What is it most likely to be? | A complete English word meaning very happy | *A piece cut from a longer word, such as gum | A drum in an orchestra | A sound a cat makes
test: Lin says «Gù» means reason, and «Gǔ» means old. Which one means old? | Gù | Gū | *Gǔ
test: The fragment «gu» sits inside the word «guide». Is «gu» a complete word here? | *No, it is a piece of a longer word | Yes, it means aunt | Yes, it means a guide
exam: Which statement is true about gu? | *Gu on its own is not an English word, but in Mandarin its tone changes its meaning | Gu means aunt in every language | Gu is a number in English
